# Build-time public configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development.
#
# ⚠️ `.env.local`, not `.env`. Vite loads BOTH, but `.env.local` is the one
# meant for machine-specific values and it takes precedence over `.env` — so a
# stale `.env` sitting next to it silently loses, which is a confusing hour to
# spend. Both are gitignored. Use one, and make it `.env.local`.
#
# Both values below are PUBLIC by design: this
# is a static site, the anon key ships to every browser, and every real security
# rule lives in Postgres RLS (supabase/migrations/). Publishing the anon key is
# the intended posture, not a leak.
#
# ⚠️ The SERVICE ROLE key is NOT here and must never be. It bypasses RLS
# entirely. It belongs only in .env.test (gitignored) for the e2e admin API, and
# in nothing that is built into the site.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-key"

# Optional. When unset the analytics snippet is omitted entirely — no empty
# script tag, no request to umami.is.
# PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=""
